+      "prompt": "Use case: style-transfer. Image1 is the EDIT TARGET: Mender-bloom's new coral cup-shaped blossom HEAD. Image2 is an original Plants vs. Zombies STYLE REFERENCE ONLY. Preserve Image1's exact cupped three-petal silhouette, all proportions, facing direction, petal folds, two notches, face placement, concerned caring brow expression, small smile, bottom sepal collar and transparent alpha. Do not add a stem or leaves. Change ONLY the surface painting: remove the conspicuous angular brushstroke bands and streaky posterized patches on the coral petals and green collar. Replace them with the original game's smooth matte shaded color, broad softly blended warm highlights and gently blended dusky shadows, like the original Sunflower face/Wall-nut surfaces in Image2. Keep enough strong dark/light modeling that the overlapping fleshy petals feel rounded, not vector-flat. Preserve the readable dark brown outline; it should be organic and confident, not an extra-thick sticker border. Keep the eyes small dark ovals with one tiny original-game-like muted glint. No glossy plastic/specular white blobs, no 3D render, no surface-grain noise, no extra facial details or props, no radial petal ring, no brown face disk. Same single head, same canvas/registration, genuinely transparent background. The result is the SAME distinctive cupped flower head with a simpler smoother original-game finish.",
+      "sha256": "f4bd5415a6da077ff55d92aebfec23ba46d12209b99172d6b37bbdee3eb5ca36",
